    "baseline_commit": "c7d2a2b439b8bfe4df323126c971167081ce881c",
    "hypothesis": "LPIPS pretrained VGG/linear parameters require gradients despite never being optimized. Freeze network parameters while preserving differentiation with respect to predicted RGB; test whether unnecessary weight-gradient convolutions cause the observed BufferTooBig.",
    "change": "Only freeze model parameters after loading pretrained LPIPS; unchanged reference photos, prediction sizes and loss formula/weights.",
    "preconditions": "GPU regression must show parameters frozen, prediction gradients nonzero and matching the trainable-weights reference, no reference gradients.",
    "plan": "Fail-first parameter regression, forward/input-gradient equivalence, then four 128px pipes runs (old/new/new/old, 500 steps, LPIPS0.01) and two 512px frozen-network runs (pipes/office,500 steps,LPIPS0.01). Reuse saved 512 failure rather than rerunning same oversized allocation.",
    "acceptance": "Same pretrained weights and numerical agreement before photo training; valid full SH3 and held-out renders at512 without BufferTooBig. No final-quality/default-weight change from a500-step feasibility test.",
